console.log(fn());","options":["undefined","It throws a SyntaxError","Asha","An empty string"],"answer":0,"explanation":"fn() is a plain call, so this is undefined in strict mode; optional chaining returns undefined instead of throwing."},{"type":"concept","question":"Which method returns a new function with this permanently fixed, without calling it?","options":["Object.create","bind","call","apply"],"answer":1,"explanation":"bind returns a new bound function; call and apply invoke the function immediately."},{"type":"scenario","question":"A class method passed as onClick={this.handleSave} throws 'Cannot read properties of undefined'. What is the most direct fix?","options":["Rename the method to start with on","Convert the class to use var","Call super() in the method","Define handleSave as a class-field arrow function or bind it in the constructor"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Passing the method detaches it from the instance. Binding or a class-field arrow keeps this pointing at the instance."},{"type":"output","question":"What does this print?","code":"const base = { role: 'user' };
